# v2.8.10 - 2026-07-14

## Improvements:
- Allow segmentation without a reference to be used with custom depths (AM-110).
- Multiscale environment will now always use hard data as reference when available, with a fallback to the color table if it has more segments (AM-30).
- Added custom behavior to multiscale post-processing tables to rewrite .tsv files after saving the scene, ensuring correct values (AM-30).
- Increased NMR histogram line width and refined variable names for clarity (AM-29).
- Adjustments to Permeability Modelling, including updates to advanced parameters range limits to account for platform-specific mathematical operation differences. (PL-3172)

## Bug fixes:
- Fixed segment list passing incorrect values and improved error handling when using segmentation as input (AM-110).
- Corrected NMR histogram colors to be transparent green with a black border (AM-29).
- Ensured the view controller color picker button retrieves the correct color from the graph (AM-29).
- Resolved an issue where the color widget was not properly receiving the alpha value (AM-29).
- Resolved issues related to Permeability Modelling. (PL-3172)
- Fix PNM extraction bug : small spacing changes lead to different networks (PL-3207)

# v2.8.8 - 2026-06-26

## Improvements:
- Improve robustness of CSV import by guessing encoding (PL-3114).
- Enhance style for dashed resolution lines (PL-3167).
- Update Pore Network Model (PNM) default values in FixedRadius and Two-phase simulations (PL-3167).
- Set Equal Angles and Constant Difference as default models (PL-3167).

## Bug fixes:
- Address a bug affecting Krel results.
- Fix corruption of Krel results during save/load operations (PL-3168).
- Resolve issues in MICP, One-phase, and other sub-resolution model simulations (PL-3168).
- Correct CDF attribution in MICP, `throat.volume` calculations in Kabs and MICP, and Kabs REV parameters (PL-3179).
- Resolve `NoneType` attribute errors during PNM simulation (PL-3151).
